# Rocketship accessibility

Reasons: `_planning/component-review-decisions.md`.

## Targets

- Minimum: WCAG 2.2 AA. Aim for AAA where it does not hurt the look or legibility.
- Text contrast: at least 4.5:1 (large text 3:1). Prefer 7:1 (large 4.5:1).
- Control edges and choice marks (tick, dash, dot): at least 3:1 against what surrounds them.
- Every control's target is at least 24×24 CSS px on its own.

## Semantics

- Use native elements: `<button>`, `<a>`, `<h1>`–`<h6>`. Avoid click handlers on `<div>` or `<span>`; if one is unavoidable, give it the correct role and ARIA.
- Every interactive component works by keyboard and shows focus.
- Add ARIA only when HTML cannot express the meaning.
- `<ul>`/`<ol>` with `list-style: none` adds `role="list"` (Safari drops list semantics otherwise).
- Never colour alone: words say what happened. Errors are semibold text plus words.

## Roles

- No default role. Static content has no role.
- For dynamic content, expose a narrow `role?` union the consumer opts into: Alert `'alert' | 'status' | 'note'`.
- A component's name never implies a role. A visual variant never maps to a live-region role.

## Headings

- Never hard-code a heading level. The consumer picks the level for the page outline; the class sets the look.

## Forms

- Every control has a `<Label for>`. A label is always a `<label>`.
- A group of controls is a `<Fieldset>` with its `legend` slot (rendered as the first child).
- Disable a group with the fieldset's native `disabled`. The legend stays readable.
- Link hint and error text with `aria-describedby` on the control. The consumer writes both ends.
- The control's `required` attribute is the source of truth. The asterisk is `aria-hidden`. Never add hidden "(required)" text. The consumer explains the asterisk once per form.
- A control in error sets `aria-invalid="true"`. Style errors from `aria-invalid`, never `:invalid`.
- Text controls never go below the page's font size (iOS zooms below 16px).
- `appearance: none` needs `@media (forced-colors: active) { appearance: auto; }`.
- A group's hint or error goes after the legend as `rs-fieldset__hint` / `rs-fieldset__error`, linked with `aria-describedby` on the fieldset. Each radio in an invalid group sets `aria-invalid="true"`. Never use `rs-field__error` inside a fieldset.
- Never show a state the control does not have: style native `:indeterminate`, set by script.

## Tables

- Header cells: `<th scope="col" class="rs-table__column-header">`, `<th scope="row" class="rs-table__row-header">`.
- The caption names the table (the `caption` slot). If a heading already names it, omit the caption and set `aria-labelledby` to the heading.
- Never make a `<table>` scroll (`display: block` strips table semantics). Wrap it in `<Scroll>`.
- Striping carries no meaning.

## Scroll regions

- Every `<Scroll>` gets `tabindex="0"`, `role="region"` and `aria-labelledby="…"` (a caption or heading). The consumer writes all three; stories always show them.

## Storybook and docs

- Interactive components have stories with keyboard examples and at least one variant that passes axe.
- Document any trade-off (a subtle focus ring, a theme contrast issue) in the component's docs or notes.
